// Title: Remote Access Tool - Simple Help Execution
// Sigma ID: 95e60a2b-4705-444b-b7da-ba0ea81a3ee2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-02-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: An adversary may use legitimate desktop support and remote access software, such as Team Viewer,
//   Go2Assist, LogMein, AmmyyAdmin, etc, to establish an interactive command and control channel to
//   target systems within networks. These services are commonly used as legitimate technical support
//   software, and may be allowed by application control within a target environment. Remote access
//   tools like VNC, Ammyy, and Teamviewer are used frequently when compared with other legitimate
//   software commonly used by adversaries. (Citation: Symantec Living off the Land)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the tool
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/slashandgrab-screen-connect-post-exploitation-in-the-wild-cve-2024-1709-cve-2024-1708
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_simple_help.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\JWrapper-Remote Access\\" or FolderPath contains "\\JWrapper-Remote Support\\") and FolderPath endswith "\\SimpleService.exe"
